---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service - Finsiva" description="Finsiva terms of service outlining the terms and conditions for using our tax calculators and tools.">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-8 dark:text-on-primary">Our Terms of Service (And Why They Actually Matter)</h1>
      <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224155-6726b3ff858f?w=1200&q=80" alt="Legal documents and contracts" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted">
        <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> July 2026</p>

        <p>Let's be honest: nobody wakes up in the morning excited to read a Terms of Service page. Usually, they're walls of dense, intimidating legalese designed to put you to sleep or make your eyes glaze over. But here at Finsiva, we believe in doing things differently. We believe that if you're trusting us with something as important as calculating your taxes, the least we can do is talk to you like a human being.</p>

        <p>This document is a mutual agreement. It sets out the rules of the road for using Finsiva. We want you to feel confident, safe, and informed when you use our tools. So, we've thrown out the jargon and rewritten our terms to be clear, understandable, and—dare we say it—maybe even a little bit relatable.</p>

        <p>Grab a coffee, settle in, and let's go over what it means to be part of the Finsiva community.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">1. Welcome to Finsiva (Acceptance of Terms)</h2>
        <p>When you use Finsiva, whether you're just browsing an article, testing out a tax calculator, or embedding our tools into your workflow, you are agreeing to these Terms of Service. Think of it like walking into a friend's house: by stepping through the door, you're agreeing to respect their space and follow their house rules.</p>
        <p>If you don't agree with anything you read here, that's completely okay! But it does mean you shouldn't use our services. Your continued use of Finsiva—whether on your phone during a commute, on a desktop at work, or anywhere else—means you're on board with these terms.</p>
        <p>We might update these terms from time to time as our tools grow and evolve. When we do, we'll update the date at the top of this page. By sticking around and using the site after those updates, you're giving us a high-five and saying, "I'm still in!"</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">2. What We Actually Do (Service Description)</h2>
        <p>Finsiva was born out of a simple frustration: taxes are confusing, and the tools to figure them out shouldn't be. We provide free, browser-based calculators, educational guides, and informational resources designed to give you a clearer picture of your tax landscape. Whether it's income tax, sales tax, property tax, capital gains, or payroll tax, we're here to help you get a solid estimate.</p>
        <p>Our tools are built for the freelancers agonizing over their quarterly payments, the small business owners trying to run payroll without pulling their hair out, the students learning about personal finance, and everyday people who just want to know where their hard-earned money is going.</p>
        <p>However—and this is a big one—we are an <em>informational</em> service. We provide estimates. We help point you in the right direction. But we are not a substitute for professional tax preparation software like TurboTax, nor are we a replacement for a certified public accountant (CPA) or a qualified tax advisor. Think of us as your knowledgeable friend who can help you do the math, not the lawyer defending you in tax court.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">3. The Big Disclaimer: We Are Not Your Accountant</h2>
        <p>We need to be crystal clear about this: <strong>THE CALCULATORS AND CONTENT ON FINSIVA ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.</strong></p>
        <p>What does that mean in plain English? It means Finsiva does not provide official tax, legal, or financial advice. The numbers our calculators spit out are estimates based on standard formulas. They are incredibly useful for planning, budgeting, and getting a general idea of your financial situation, but they should never, ever be the sole basis for your actual tax filing decisions.</p>
        
        <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-0">A Real-World Scenario: The Overconfident Freelancer</h3>
            <p>Imagine a freelance graphic designer named Alex. Alex uses Finsiva to estimate their end-of-year tax bill and gets a number: $4,500. Thrilled, Alex sets aside exactly $4,500 and files their taxes without a second thought. But Alex forgot to account for a specific local business tax in their county, and our calculator—being a general tool—didn't know Alex lived in that specific county. Alex ends up owing $5,200 and getting hit with a late fee by the IRS.</p>
            <p><strong>The takeaway:</strong> Alex should have used Finsiva to get a baseline estimate, but then verified those numbers with a tax professional or official IRS software before writing the check. Finsiva is not responsible for penalties, interest, or surprise tax bills. Always double-check.</p>
        </div>

        <p>Tax authorities might use different rounding methods, apply obscure transitional rules, or redefine terms in ways our calculators can't predict. You are fully responsible for verifying your results against official forms before you hit "submit" on your tax return.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">4. Accuracy, Updates, and the Moving Target of Tax Law</h2>
        <p>Tax laws change constantly. Politicians pass new bills, tax brackets are adjusted for inflation, and obscure loopholes are closed (or opened). We work incredibly hard to keep our calculators and content up-to-date with these shifting rules. Our team is always monitoring legislative changes to ensure our tools reflect the current reality.</p>
        <p>But we are human, and the tax code is a beast. We cannot guarantee that every single piece of information on Finsiva is 100% current or error-free at all times. There is often a lag between when a new tax rule is announced and when it is officially implemented, and there may be a slight delay before we can update our code to reflect those changes.</p>
        <p>If you're making major financial decisions, always cross-reference our tools with the official resources provided by your local tax authority (like the IRS, HMRC, CRA, or ATO).</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">5. Why We Can't Guarantee Exact Results</h2>
        <p>No calculator on the internet can guarantee a perfect match with your final tax bill, and Finsiva is no exception. Why? Because taxes are wildly complex and deeply personal.</p>
        <p>Our calculators use simplified models. They are fantastic at doing the heavy lifting for standard scenarios, but they cannot capture every single nuance of your life. We might not know about that obscure tax credit you qualify for because you installed energy-efficient windows, or that you fall under the Alternative Minimum Tax (AMT), or that you have complex capital loss carryovers from three years ago.</p>
        <p>If your financial situation involves multiple income streams, international investments, complex business structures, or major life changes, you absolutely need to seek professional advice. Our tools will get you in the right ballpark, but only a pro can get you to home plate safely.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">6. Your Role and Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>This relationship is a two-way street. We provide the tools, but you are the one behind the wheel.</p>
        <p>You are entirely responsible for the information you type into our calculators. If you enter your income as $50,000 when it's actually $150,000, the results will be wrong. Garbage in, garbage out. You are also responsible for the choices you make based on our estimates.</p>
        <p>Furthermore, we expect you to be a good citizen of the Finsiva community. You agree not to use our calculators for nefarious purposes. This includes trying to generate fake financial statements for a loan application, using our tools to figure out how to illegally evade taxes, or misleading third parties.</p>
        <p>We are here to help people understand their finances, not to facilitate fraud. If we discover that someone is abusing our services, we reserve the right to block their access permanently.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">7. How We Might Change the Service</h2>
        <p>Finsiva is a living, breathing platform. We're constantly adding new calculators, tweaking designs, and improving our algorithms. This means that the site will change over time.</p>
        <p>We reserve the right to modify, suspend, or even discontinue certain parts of the Service without prior notice. We might decide to retire an old, rarely used calculator, or we might fundamentally change how a tool looks and feels. While we will always try to give you a heads-up if we're making a massive change that could disrupt your workflow, we can't guarantee that the site will look exactly the same tomorrow as it does today, or that a specific tool will be available forever.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">8. Limitation of Liability (The Legal Armor)</h2>
        <p>This is standard for almost any website, but it's important. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Finsiva (and our team members, founders, and partners) shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages that happen as a result of using our tools.</p>
        <p>If you make a bad investment because our capital gains calculator gave you an estimate that didn't factor in a sudden market crash, we are not liable for your lost profits. We are not liable for data loss, damage to your reputation, or any other intangible losses. Our liability is strictly limited by the law of the land.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">9. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>If things ever get serious and there is a legal dispute, these Terms of Service will be governed by the laws of the jurisdiction where Finsiva is headquartered, ignoring any conflict of law rules. That means any legal proceedings will take place in our local courts.</p>
        <p>If you're using Finsiva from another country, that's awesome! We love our international users. But please remember that you are still responsible for complying with your own local laws, including how you handle data and report your taxes.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">10. Dispute Resolution: Let's Talk It Out First</h2>
        <p>Lawsuits are stressful, expensive, and generally terrible for everyone involved. If you have a problem with Finsiva, we want to fix it directly with you.</p>
        <p>If you're upset about something, please email us at support@finsiva.com. We promise that a real human being will read your email, and we will work in good faith to resolve your issue as quickly and fairly as possible.</p>
        <p>If, for some reason, we simply cannot reach an agreement, any formal disputes will need to be resolved through binding arbitration or the appropriate courts, as allowed by law. By using Finsiva, you also agree to wave any right to participate in a class-action lawsuit against us. Let's keep things one-on-one.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">11. Intellectual Property (Don't Steal Our Stuff)</h2>
        <p>We've put thousands of hours into coding, designing, and writing the content on Finsiva. It's our pride and joy. All the text, code, logos, designs, and tools on this site are the intellectual property of Finsiva.</p>
        <p>You are more than welcome to print out a calculator result for your personal records, or share a link to one of our articles on social media. But you may not scrape our site, copy our code, steal our designs, or take our content and publish it on your own website as if it were your own. If you want to partner with us or use our tools commercially, just reach out and ask! We're friendly, but we will protect our hard work.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">12. User Conduct: Just Be Cool</h2>
        <p>The rules for using Finsiva are simple: use it for what it's meant for, and don't be a jerk.</p>
        <p>You agree not to try and hack our systems, overwhelm our servers with automated bots, or scrape our data at a massive scale. If our monitoring systems detect that your IP address is trying to brute-force our site or run malicious scripts, we will block you immediately without warning.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">13. Termination</h2>
        <p>We hope it never comes to this, but we reserve the right to cut off your access to Finsiva at any time, for any reason, without notice. Usually, this only happens if someone is blatantly violating these terms or trying to harm the site or other users.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">14. Frequently Asked Questions About Our Terms</h2>
        
        <div class="space-y-4 my-8">
            <details class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-4">
                <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Do you sell the financial data I type into the calculators?</summary>
                <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                    Absolutely not. Most of our calculators run entirely in your browser, meaning the numbers you type never even reach our servers. For the tools that do require server processing, we do not store, track, or sell your personal financial data to third parties. Your numbers are your business.
                </div>
            </details>
            
            <details class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-4">
                <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Can I use your calculators for my clients if I'm an accountant?</summary>
                <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                    Yes, you can use our tools as a quick reference during a client consultation. However, you may not present our tools as your own proprietary software, and you cannot rely on our estimates as the final calculation for their actual tax filing. You must use certified professional software for their actual returns.
                </div>
            </details>

            <details class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-4">
                <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What happens if the calculator gives me the wrong number and I get audited?</summary>
                <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                    As outlined in Section 3 and Section 8, Finsiva provides estimates for informational purposes only. We are not liable for any penalties, audits, or fees incurred because of discrepancies between our estimate and your final tax bill. It is always your responsibility to verify numbers with a professional before filing.
                </div>
            </details>
            
            <details class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-4">
                <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Can I link to your calculators from my blog?</summary>
                <div class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                    Yes! We love it when people share our tools. You are welcome to link directly to any calculator or article on Finsiva. You just can't frame our site within yours or copy/paste our code to host the calculator yourself.
                </div>
            </details>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">15. Let's Stay in Touch</h2>
        <p>If you've actually read this far, congratulations! You have an incredible attention span. We hope this document made our terms a little easier to digest and understand.</p>
        <p>If you have any questions at all about these Terms of Service, how our calculators work, or just want to say hello, we are always here. Contact us at <a href="/contact/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">support@finsiva.com</a> or visit our <a href="/about/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">About</a> page to learn more about the humans behind the site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>